You calmed down and looked over yourself one more time. You looked like an ordinary wolf, just a little larger. It's unlikely that your pursuers would tell the difference in the dark. You just hoped that you left no tracks by the enclosure, and that they wouldn’t have hounds to sniff you out.
Suddenly your attention was drawn to a cell phone hanging around your neck. You hastily tore it off and hid it in the grass. Just in time! 
 You heard voices in the alley. Flashlight beams were sliding over the roads, enclosures, and grass. Soon three men came up to the enclosure you were in. You recognized one of them. The old man was Olaf, the zoo watchman, and two armed policemen were with him.
"Are you sure that everything is normal, old man?" harshly asked one of the cops. "Are your animals all here?" They lit the enclosure with the beams. It lit up the pack and you.
Olaf reluctantly looked inside the enclosure.  
"Yes, everything is fine. The animals would alert me if something was wrong. They are much smarter than you assholes."
The police officer just hemmed.
"Fine, Swen, let's get out of here. It looks like everything is ok."
The officers turned around and went off. Olaf continued to look at the wolves for some time and then he also left.